\begin{abstract}
This document presents the full production-grade C++20 implementation of the 
SIE-ASTRO v4.0 simulation core. The engine integrates an OpenMP-parallelized 
relativistic Boris particle pusher, a staggered Yee-mesh constrained transport 
electromagnetic solver, and an AES-256-GCM cryptographic telemetry pipeline. 
All components are optimized for high-performance distributed execution and 
machine-precision divergence control. The complete source code, build system, 
and execution driver are included for laboratory validation and deployment.
\end{abstract}

